IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mlr-core`

-- SCHEDULE 6 -- MEANING OF "RELEVANT REQUIREMENT" (S.I. 2017/692, lines 3256-3348 of the plain-text
-- rendering, which is not the official text and is not verified against it).
--
-- WHAT IT IS FOR.  Regulation 75 (part mlr4, line 2451) says: "For the purposes of this Part,
-- 'relevant requirement' has the meaning given in Schedule 6."  Part 9 lets a designated supervisory authority
-- impose a civil penalty on a person it is satisfied has contravened a relevant requirement (regulation 76(1), line 2454)
-- and makes it a criminal offence to contravene one (regulation 86(1), line 2644).  SEAM S-17, answered here for part mlr4.
--
-- THE SHAPE OF THE SCHEDULE.  A chapeau (printed paragraph 1) with three limbs, then fourteen printed
-- paragraphs of lists (printed paragraphs 2 to 15).  THE RENDERING PRINTS NO NUMBER AFTER THE CHAPEAU
-- (FORK S6-F1 in NOTES.md).  The chapeau cites "paragraph 2", "paragraph 3" and "paragraph 4" (the
-- three lists of Articles), and "paragraphs 5 to 13" (the lists of regulations).  This module numbers
-- the printed paragraphs 2 to 15 in the order they are printed, which matches the chapeau for 2, 3 and 4.
-- Printed paragraphs 14 (regulations 66 to 78) and 15 (regulation 84(1)) lie AFTER the last number the
-- chapeau cites.  Whether the chapeau's "5 to 13" reaches them (because two of the printed paragraphs
-- carry letters in the official text, which this rendering does not show) cannot be told from the
-- rendering; a requirement in printed paragraph 14 or 15 therefore answers NOTHING under limb (b), not
-- TRUE and not FALSE.
--
-- THE FACTS ASKED.  The Schedule is about a requirement: which instrument imposes it (the funds transfer
-- regulation, these Regulations, or the UK auctioning regulations), which provision (an Article or a
-- regulation number, and a paragraph of it, or none), and on whom it is imposed (limb (a) depends on
-- the role of the payment service provider; limb (b) excludes supervisory authorities, registering
-- authorities and auction platforms; limb (c) is about auction platforms).  A requirement "imposed in or
-- under" a listed provision is read as a requirement of that provision, in or under; the rendering lists
-- some provisions with "imposed in" and some with "imposed under", and limb (b) says "in or under" for
-- all of the lists of regulations.

-- src:3256 | SCHEDULE 6 — Meaning of “relevant requirement”
§ `Schedule 6 -- the facts and the lists`

-- The three instruments the Schedule reaches.  Anything else is "another instrument".
DECLARE `sch 6 instrument` IS ONE OF
    `sch 6 the funds transfer regulation`
    `sch 6 these Regulations`
    `sch 6 the UK auctioning regulations`
    `sch 6 another instrument`

-- On whom the requirement is imposed.  Limb (a) turns on the payment service provider's role;
-- limb (b) excludes three kinds of bearer; limb (c) is about auction platforms.
DECLARE `sch 6 bearer` IS ONE OF
    `sch 6 the payment service provider of a payer`
    `sch 6 the payment service provider of a payee`
    `sch 6 the payment service provider of an intermediary`
    `sch 6 a supervisory authority`
    `sch 6 a registering authority`
    `sch 6 an auction platform`
    `sch 6 any other person`

-- The requirement asked about.  `paragraph` is "" when the question names the Article or regulation
-- as a whole without a paragraph of it.
DECLARE `sch 6 requirement` HAS
    `instrument`  IS A `sch 6 instrument`
    `number`      IS A STRING           -- an Article or regulation number as printed, e.g. "28", "30ZA", "45ZA"
    `paragraph`   IS A STRING           -- a paragraph of it as printed without brackets, e.g. "11", "10A"; "" for none
    `bearer`      IS A `sch 6 bearer`

-- One entry of one of the Schedule's lists: a whole provision (no paragraphs) or some paragraphs of it.
DECLARE `sch 6 listed provision` HAS
    `instrument`  IS A `sch 6 instrument`
    `number`      IS A STRING
    `paragraphs`  IS A LIST OF STRING   -- empty: the whole of the Article or regulation

GIVEN n IS A STRING
GIVETH A `sch 6 listed provision`
`sch 6 listed: Article` MEANS `sch 6 listed provision` OF `sch 6 the funds transfer regulation`, n, EMPTY

GIVEN n IS A STRING
GIVETH A `sch 6 listed provision`
`sch 6 listed: regulation` MEANS `sch 6 listed provision` OF `sch 6 these Regulations`, n, EMPTY

GIVEN n IS A STRING
      ps IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A `sch 6 listed provision`
`sch 6 listed: paragraphs of regulation` MEANS `sch 6 listed provision` OF `sch 6 these Regulations`, n, ps

GIVEN n IS A STRING
GIVETH A `sch 6 listed provision`
`sch 6 listed: UK auctioning regulation` MEANS `sch 6 listed provision` OF `sch 6 the UK auctioning regulations`, n, EMPTY

