-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Matching an asked requirement against a list.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- A listed entry covers the asked requirement outright: the same instrument, the same Article or
-- regulation number, and either the entry is the whole provision or it lists the asked paragraph.
GIVEN row IS A `sch 6 listed provision`
      ask IS A `sch 6 requirement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 6 the listed provision covers the requirement` MEANS
        row's `instrument` EQUALS ask's `instrument`
    AND row's `number` EQUALS ask's `number`
    AND (    null (row's `paragraphs`)
          OR elem (ask's `paragraph`) (row's `paragraphs`))

-- The asked requirement names the provision as a whole ("") and the entry lists only some paragraphs of it.
GIVEN row IS A `sch 6 listed provision`
      ask IS A `sch 6 requirement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 6 the listed provision covers only some paragraphs of the one asked about` MEANS
        row's `instrument` EQUALS ask's `instrument`
    AND row's `number` EQUALS ask's `number`
    AND ask's `paragraph` EQUALS ""
    AND NOT (null (row's `paragraphs`))

-- Against a whole list: TRUE if an entry covers it; NOTHING if the question left out a paragraph and an
-- entry lists only some; FALSE if no entry has that Article or regulation (the list is introduced by "those
-- imposed in" and the whole definition by "means").
GIVEN rows IS A LIST OF `sch 6 listed provision`
      ask IS A `sch 6 requirement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 the requirement is within the list` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF any (GIVEN row YIELD `sch 6 the listed provision covers the requirement` row ask) rows
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF any (GIVEN row YIELD `sch 6 the listed provision covers only some paragraphs of the one asked about` row ask) rows
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the question names the provision without a paragraph and the list covers only some of its paragraphs
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means" (the list does not contain the provision)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The chapeau: "For the purposes of Part 9 of these Regulations, 'relevant requirement' means— ..."
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Limb (a): a requirement imposed by the funds transfer regulation, specified in paragraph 2 for
-- the payment service provider of a payer, paragraph 3 for a payee, paragraph 4 for an intermediary.
-- src:3257 | For the purposes of Part 9 of these Regulations, “relevant requirement” means—
-- src:3258 | (a) a requirement imposed by the funds transfer regulation specified—
-- src:3259 | (i) in relation to a payment service provider of a payer, in paragraph 2;
-- src:3260 | (ii) in relation to a payment service provider of a payee, in paragraph 3;
-- src:3261 | (iii) in relation to the payment service provider of an intermediary, in paragraph 4.
@ref sch 6 para 1(a) (src:3257-3261)
GIVEN ask IS A `sch 6 requirement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 para 1(a) the requirement is imposed by the funds transfer regulation and specified in paragraph 2, 3 or 4` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF ask's `instrument` EQUALS `sch 6 the funds transfer regulation` AND ask's `bearer` EQUALS `sch 6 the payment service provider of a payer`
        THEN `sch 6 the requirement is within the list` (`sch 6 para 2 the listed Articles`) ask
        IF ask's `instrument` EQUALS `sch 6 the funds transfer regulation` AND ask's `bearer` EQUALS `sch 6 the payment service provider of a payee`
        THEN `sch 6 the requirement is within the list` (`sch 6 para 3 the listed Articles`) ask
        IF ask's `instrument` EQUALS `sch 6 the funds transfer regulation` AND ask's `bearer` EQUALS `sch 6 the payment service provider of an intermediary`
        THEN `sch 6 the requirement is within the list` (`sch 6 para 4 the listed Articles`) ask
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means" and "a requirement imposed by the funds transfer regulation specified (i) in relation to a payment service provider of a payer, ..." (the requirement is not one of the funds transfer regulation imposed on a payer's, a payee's or an intermediary's payment service provider)

-- Limb (b): a requirement imposed (otherwise than on supervisory authorities, registering authorities or
-- auction platforms) in or under the regulations specified in paragraphs 5 to 13.
-- Printed paragraphs 5 to 13 are within the range.  Printed paragraphs 14 and 15 are after the last number
-- the chapeau cites and answer NOTHING (fork S6-F1).
-- src:3262 | (b) a requirement imposed (otherwise than on supervisory authorities, registering authorities or auction platforms) in or under the regulations specified in paragraphs 5 to 13;
@ref sch 6 para 1(b) (src:3262)
GIVEN ask IS A `sch 6 requirement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 para 1(b) the requirement is imposed in or under the regulations specified in paragraphs 5 to 13` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (ask's `instrument` EQUALS `sch 6 these Regulations`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means" and "in or under the regulations specified in paragraphs 5 to 13" (the requirement is not of these Regulations)
        IF    ask's `bearer` EQUALS `sch 6 a supervisory authority`
           OR ask's `bearer` EQUALS `sch 6 a registering authority`
           OR ask's `bearer` EQUALS `sch 6 an auction platform`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means" and "otherwise than on supervisory authorities, registering authorities or auction platforms"
        IF `sch 6 the requirement is within the list` (`sch 6 para 5 the listed regulations`) ask EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `sch 6 the requirement is within the list` (`sch 6 para 6 the listed regulations`) ask EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `sch 6 the requirement is within the list` (`sch 6 para 7 the listed regulations`) ask EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `sch 6 the requirement is within the list` (`sch 6 para 8 the listed regulations`) ask EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `sch 6 the requirement is within the list` (`sch 6 para 9 the listed regulations`) ask EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `sch 6 the requirement is within the list` (`sch 6 para 10 the listed regulations`) ask EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `sch 6 the requirement is within the list` (`sch 6 para 11 the listed regulations`) ask EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `sch 6 the requirement is within the list` (`sch 6 para 12 the listed regulations`) ask EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `sch 6 the requirement is within the list` (`sch 6 para 13 the listed regulations`) ask EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF     `sch 6 the requirement is within the list` (`sch 6 para 5 the listed regulations`) ask EQUALS NOTHING
            OR `sch 6 the requirement is within the list` (`sch 6 para 6 the listed regulations`) ask EQUALS NOTHING
            OR `sch 6 the requirement is within the list` (`sch 6 para 7 the listed regulations`) ask EQUALS NOTHING
            OR `sch 6 the requirement is within the list` (`sch 6 para 8 the listed regulations`) ask EQUALS NOTHING
            OR `sch 6 the requirement is within the list` (`sch 6 para 9 the listed regulations`) ask EQUALS NOTHING
            OR `sch 6 the requirement is within the list` (`sch 6 para 10 the listed regulations`) ask EQUALS NOTHING
            OR `sch 6 the requirement is within the list` (`sch 6 para 11 the listed regulations`) ask EQUALS NOTHING
            OR `sch 6 the requirement is within the list` (`sch 6 para 12 the listed regulations`) ask EQUALS NOTHING
            OR `sch 6 the requirement is within the list` (`sch 6 para 13 the listed regulations`) ask EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the question names a regulation without a paragraph and the list covers only some of its paragraphs
        IF     `sch 6 the requirement is within the list` (`sch 6 para 14 the listed regulations`) ask EQUALS JUST TRUE
            OR `sch 6 the requirement is within the list` (`sch 6 para 14 the listed regulations`) ask EQUALS NOTHING
            OR `sch 6 the requirement is within the list` (`sch 6 para 15 the listed regulations`) ask EQUALS JUST TRUE
            OR `sch 6 the requirement is within the list` (`sch 6 para 15 the listed regulations`) ask EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the provision is in the 14th or 15th printed paragraph, after the last number ("13") the chapeau cites; the rendering prints no paragraph numbers, so whether "paragraphs 5 to 13" reaches it is not shown (fork S6-F1)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means" and "in or under the regulations specified in paragraphs 5 to 13" (the provision is in none of the lists)

-- Limb (c): the following requirements imposed on auction platforms.
-- (i) and (ii): regulations 17 and 37 of the UK auctioning regulations (the whole regulation; the
-- Schedule says "the customer due diligence requirements in regulation 17" and "the monitoring and
-- record keeping requirements of regulation 37", and the regulations themselves are not among the sources).
-- (iii): regulations 18 to 21 or 24 of these Regulations.  The range "18 to 21" names 18, 19, 20 and 21;
-- whether it reaches the lettered regulations 18A and 19A that sit between them is not stated (FORK S6-F2 in NOTES.md).
-- (iv): any requirement imposed under the regulations of the last list.
-- src:3263 | (c) the following requirements imposed on auction platforms—
-- src:3264 | (i) the customer due diligence requirements in regulation 17 of the UK auctioning regulations;
-- src:3265 | (ii) the monitoring and record keeping requirements of regulation 37 of the UK auctioning regulations; or
-- src:3266 | (iii) the requirements imposed in regulations 18 to 21 or 24 of these Regulations;
-- src:3267 | (iv) any requirement imposed under regulations 66, 69(2), 70(7), 77(2) and (6) or 78(2) or (5) of these Regulations.
@ref sch 6 para 1(c) (src:3263-3267)
GIVEN ask IS A `sch 6 requirement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 para 1(c) the requirement is one of those imposed on auction platforms` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (ask's `bearer` EQUALS `sch 6 an auction platform`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means" and "the following requirements imposed on auction platforms" (the requirement is not imposed on an auction platform)
        IF     ask's `instrument` EQUALS `sch 6 the UK auctioning regulations`
           AND (ask's `number` EQUALS "17" OR ask's `number` EQUALS "37")
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF     ask's `instrument` EQUALS `sch 6 these Regulations`
           AND (    ask's `number` EQUALS "18" OR ask's `number` EQUALS "19" OR ask's `number` EQUALS "20"
                 OR ask's `number` EQUALS "21" OR ask's `number` EQUALS "24")
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF     ask's `instrument` EQUALS `sch 6 these Regulations`
           AND (ask's `number` EQUALS "18A" OR ask's `number` EQUALS "19A")
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "regulations 18 to 21" names the numbers 18 to 21 and the text does not say whether the lettered regulations 18A and 19A between them are in the range (fork S6-F2)
        IF `sch 6 the requirement is within the list` (`sch 6 para 1(c)(iv) the listed regulations`) ask EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `sch 6 the requirement is within the list` (`sch 6 para 1(c)(iv) the listed regulations`) ask EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the question names the regulation without a paragraph and the list covers only some of its paragraphs
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means" and "the following requirements imposed on auction platforms" (the provision is in none of the lists of limb (c))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Gathered by hand (ruling E1, option B, as guidance for gathering a legal effect's routes by hand
-- only; each limb also has its own function above, option C): a relevant requirement is one that any
-- limb of the chapeau covers.  "means" closes the definition, so a requirement that no limb covers is
-- the text's no.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- SEAM S-17 (answering): part mlr4, reg 75, asks `sch 6 the provision is a relevant requirement`.
@ref sch 6 para 1 (the chapeau and limbs (a) to (c) together)
GIVEN ask IS A `sch 6 requirement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 the provision is a relevant requirement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     `sch 6 para 1(a) the requirement is imposed by the funds transfer regulation and specified in paragraph 2, 3 or 4` ask EQUALS JUST TRUE
            OR `sch 6 para 1(b) the requirement is imposed in or under the regulations specified in paragraphs 5 to 13` ask EQUALS JUST TRUE
            OR `sch 6 para 1(c) the requirement is one of those imposed on auction platforms` ask EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF     `sch 6 para 1(a) the requirement is imposed by the funds transfer regulation and specified in paragraph 2, 3 or 4` ask EQUALS JUST FALSE
           AND `sch 6 para 1(b) the requirement is imposed in or under the regulations specified in paragraphs 5 to 13` ask EQUALS JUST FALSE
           AND `sch 6 para 1(c) the requirement is one of those imposed on auction platforms` ask EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'relevant requirement' means—" and no limb covers the requirement
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): a limb answered NOTHING because the text does not say whether a requirement in the 14th or 15th printed list or in regulation 18A or 19A is within the range the chapeau or limb (c)(iii) names (forks S6-F1 and S6-F2), and no other limb covers the requirement
